.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt PREBSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm prebsd
.Nd fetch and boot an old system image on SIMH
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fk
.Op Fl b Ar sequence
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl r Ar tries
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Ar image
.Op Ar command
.Nm
.Fl l
.Nm
.Fl S Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
fetches the files of a disk image, starts the SIMH simulator on its configuration, and drives the
simulated console over telnet through the boot, so that the system comes up without a person at the keyboard.
.Pp
.Ar image
is a name from
.Pa images.json
(Research Unix V4 to V7, 32V, TOPS-10 6.03 on the KA10 and the KI10), a SIMH
.Pa .ini ,
or a single-image JSON manifest with the fields of an
.Pa images.json
entry.
.Pp
The steps:
.Bl -enum
.It
Each file of the image that is missing from
.Pa images/
is downloaded and checked against its SHA-256.
A downloaded file is also kept as it came in
.Pa mirror/images/ ,
and is used from there when the download fails or the upstream is gone.
A file that differs from the manifest is moved aside as
.Pa NAME.modified ,
never overwritten.
.It
A disk that the image makes from a tape itself (the manifest's
.Ql install
script, when its
.Ql needs
file is missing) is made; the result is kept in
.Pa mirror/built/ .
.It
The simulator is started: the one in
.Pa simh/bin/
(made by
.Xr build-simh 1 ) ,
else
.Ev SIMH ,
else the one on the
.Ev PATH .
.It
The boot sequence of the manifest,
.Ql SEND>EXPECT
pairs separated by
.Ql | ,
is typed at the console.
If a step does not show its text in time the simulator is started again, up to the image's
.Ql retries
times: the PDP-10 boot sometimes hangs after the
.Ql %DPA
lines.
.It
For Unix, the shell is reached and the terminal made mixed case (V7's console driver uppercases).
Another system is up when its
.Ql ready
text appears.
.It
The optional
.Ar command
is typed and the console output shown.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar sequence
Use this boot sequence instead of the image's.
.It Fl f
Only fetch the files.
.It Fl k
Leave the simulator running when the boot is done.
Its console stays connected to a process that only logs it (to
.Pa simh/run/NAME.console ) ;
other telnet lines, such as the DC lines of the PDP-10, stay available.
.It Fl l
List the images.
.It Fl p Ar port
The telnet port of the console, if not the ini's
.Ql set console telnet= .
.It Fl r Ar tries
Tries when the boot hangs.
.It Fl S Ar image
Stop an image started with
.Fl k .
.It Fl t Ar seconds
How long to wait for each step; the default is 90.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PREBSD_MIRROR
.It Ev SIMH
The simulator to run, instead of the image's.
.It Ev PREBSD_MIRROR
The directory of the local copies (default
.Pa mirror ) .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "simh/run/NAME.pid"
.It Pa images.json
the manifest; the
.Pa ini/
directory holds the SIMH configurations
.It Pa images/
the disks and tapes
.It Pa mirror/
local copies of the downloads, the simulator sources and the built disks
.It Pa simh/bin/
the simulators made by
.Xr build-simh 1
.It Pa simh/run/NAME.pid
the simulator and console ports of an image started with
.Fl k
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 if the system came up, 1 if not.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fetch 1 ,
.Xr build-simh 1
